{
  "id": "subarray-sum-equals-k",
  "questionId": "subarray-sum-equals-k",
  "slug": "subarray-sum-equals-k",
  "title": "Subarray Sum Equals K",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Hash map",
  "patterns": [
    "hash map",
    "prefix sum"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "negative numbers rule out a sliding window, since growing or shrinking the window doesn't move the sum in a predictable direction. what other way could you express 'the sum of a subarray'?",
    "the sum of nums[i..j] can be written as prefixSum[j] - prefixSum[i-1]. if you're standing at index j, what prefix sum value would you need to have seen before to make that difference equal k?",
    "you need prefixSum[j] - k to have occurred as a prefix sum at some earlier index. keep a running hash map of how many times each prefix sum value has been seen so far",
    "at each index, add to your count however many times (prefixSum so far - k) has already occurred, then record the current prefix sum in the map"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "trying to adapt the sliding window technique from Minimum Size Subarray Sum, which breaks with negative numbers",
    "forgetting to seed the hash map with prefixSum 0 occurring once (for subarrays starting at index 0 that sum exactly to k)",
    "checking for prefixSum + k instead of prefixSum - k, or updating the map before doing the lookup for the current index"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array of integers, which may include negative numbers,\nand an integer `k`.\n\n**Count how many contiguous subarrays sum to exactly k.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= nums.length <= 2 * 10^4",
      "-1000 <= nums[i] <= 1000",
      "-10^7 <= k <= 10^7"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "k = 0 with zeroes in the array",
      "negative numbers that let a longer subarray sum back down to k",
      "no subarray sums to k (answer 0)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
